{
  "esm": "0.6.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "GEOSFP_I3_loader",
    "description": "Pure-I/O data loader for GEOS-FP (I3 collection): 3-hourly instantaneous 3-D temperature/humidity fields plus surface pressure on the native 0.3125°×0.25° global longitude/latitude grid, from the GEOS-Chem GEOS_FP 0.25x0.3125 archive.\n\nThis is one loader half of the geosfp loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§7; bead esm-3nc.2, following the esm-3nc.1 era5/wrf pattern). It is PURE I/O: it declares its source (url_template), the file variables it reads (with units), its temporal cadence, and its NATIVE grid expressed as a GDD Grid with a geographic (longlat/WGS84) crs descriptor. It performs NO reprojection and NO regridding — those are per-variable concerns of the regridding model (components/earthsci_data/geosfp.esm), which references this file as a subsystem via {\"ref\": \"./geosfp_i3_loader.esm\"} under the subsystem key GEOSFP_I3.\n\nThe removed co-located blocks: the old DataLoaderSpatial block (proj4 crs string / grid_type / staggering / resolution / extent) is replaced by the GDD `grid` (family + crs + dimensions + extents); the old per-loader `regridding` block (fill_value / extrapolation) is gone — regridding is declared per-variable on the model (geosfp.esm `regrid`). Because a `temporal` block is present, this loader seeds DISCRETE cadence (ess-v9a.5): the runtime refreshes the file buffers on its update schedule.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl (GEOSFPFileSet, filetype=I3). Split out of the pre-migration components/earthsci_data/geosfp.esm (esm-1c6s).",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "meteorology",
      "geos_fp",
      "global",
      "data_loader",
      "pure-io",
      "longlat"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "NASA GMAO / GEOS-Chem",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.2)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "GEOS-FP data archived for GEOS-Chem classic. NASA Global Modeling and Assimilation Office (GMAO). AWS S3 mirror: s3://geos-chem/GEOS_{domain}/GEOS_FP/. See http://geoschemdata.wustl.edu/ExtData/ for current domain and file-type options.",
        "url": "http://geoschemdata.wustl.edu/ExtData/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Molod, A., Takacs, L., Suarez, M., and Bacmeister, J. (2015). Development of the GEOS-5 atmospheric general circulation model: evolution from MERRA to MERRA2. Geosci. Model Dev., 8, 1339–1356.",
        "doi": "10.5194/gmd-8-1339-2015"
      },
      {
        "citation": "GEOS-Chem vertical grid documentation: https://wiki.seas.harvard.edu/geos-chem/index.php/GEOS-Chem_vertical_grids",
        "url": "https://wiki.seas.harvard.edu/geos-chem/index.php/GEOS-Chem_vertical_grids"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl (GEOSFPFileSet, GEOSFP constructor, Ap/Bp hybrid grid coefficients, geosfp_staggering). Test: test/geosfp_test.jl. Docs: docs present in pinned commit."
      }
    ]
  },
  "data_loaders": {
    "GEOSFP_I3": {
      "kind": "grid",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "https://geos-chem.s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/GEOS_0.25x0.3125/GEOS_FP/{date:%Y}/{date:%m}/GEOSFP.{date:%Y%m%d}.I3.025x03125.nc"
      },
      "temporal": {
        "start": "2013-01-01T00:00:00Z",
        "file_period": "P1D",
        "frequency": "PT3H",
        "records_per_file": 8,
        "time_variable": "time"
      },
      "grid": {
        "family": "cartesian",
        "crs": {
          "projection": "longlat",
          "datum": "WGS84"
        },
        "description": "Native GEOS-FP grid: regular global 0.3125°×0.25° (lon×lat) longitude/latitude lattice on 72 hybrid-sigma layers (lev index 1=surface … 72=top, layer centers, unit spacing). Geographic (unprojected) longlat/WGS84 crs — the regridding model applies the longlat IDENTITY reprojection (ESD reprojection/longlat.esm, esd-47z.1). Migrated from the loader's former DataLoaderSpatial block (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1); the loader describes this grid but performs no reprojection or regridding. Dimension cell counts resolve from the source dataset at load time; the documented native geometry is lon ∈ [-180°, 180°] (1152 cells, 0.3125°), lat ∈ [-90°, 90°] (720 cells, 0.25°), lev = 72 hybrid-sigma layers.",
        "dimensions": [
          "lon",
          "lat",
          "lev"
        ],
        "extents": {
          "lon": {
            "n": 1152,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "lat": {
            "n": 720,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          },
          "lev": {
            "n": 72,
            "spacing": "uniform"
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "T": {
          "file_variable": "T",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Air temperature (K). 3-hourly instantaneous 3D field at hybrid pressure levels. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "QV": {
          "file_variable": "QV",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Specific humidity of water vapor (kg/kg). 3-hourly instantaneous 3D field. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "PS": {
          "file_variable": "PS",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Surface pressure (Pa). 3-hourly instantaneous 2D field (lat×lon only, no lev dimension). Used for hybrid pressure calculation P = Ap[lev] + Bp[lev]*PS. Clamp extrapolation."
        }
      },
      "reference": {
        "citation": "GEOS-FP I3 collection. NASA GMAO.",
        "url": "http://geoschemdata.wustl.edu/ExtData/"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "geos_fp",
          "meteorology",
          "instantaneous",
          "3-hourly",
          "3d"
        ],
        "earthscidata_source": "src/geosfp.jl::GEOSFPFileSet (filetype=I3)",
        "filetype": "I3",
        "domain": "0.25x0.3125",
        "time_instant_note": "I3 records are instantaneous (not time-averaged): 00:00, 03:00, 06:00, 09:00, 12:00, 15:00, 18:00, 21:00 UTC (Delta_Time=030000, Start_Time=00:00:00.0). PS is a 2D variable with lon and lat dimensions but no lev dimension.",
        "native_resolution_deg": {
          "longitude": 0.3125,
          "latitude": 0.25
        },
        "native_extent": {
          "longitude": [
            -180.0,
            180.0
          ],
          "latitude": [
            -90.0,
            90.0
          ],
          "lev_layer_index": [
            1,
            72
          ]
        },
        "regridding_provenance": "Former co-located data_loaders.regridding block (fill_value=0.0, extrapolation=clamp) removed in the 0.6.0 hard break; regridding is now declared per-variable on the GEOSFP model `regrid` (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§5.2).",
        "crs_provenance": "Former DataLoaderSpatial.crs '+proj=longlat +datum=WGS84 +no_defs' is now the structured GDD grid.crs {projection: longlat, datum: WGS84}."
      }
    }
  }
}
